data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":85,"item_id":"rs_08a008f2f2618944016ac91ff586a88197a87aa1f80bf9984c","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering migration and UI tests**\n\nI’m thinking about whether I need to perform migration tests and UI tests through bash. Should I write a new file or just edit and append at the end? Maybe I can reuse the UI test setup to keep things efficient. New tests could add to existing ones as long as they’re unique. It might be easier if I create a new `archive.test` file that includes both UI and migration tests."}

